```

july_scp vs july_water_air = -0.71

👉 SCP is almost identical to HSF in redundancy strength
👉 but weaker than MSD (which was -0.81)

SCP = “was any part of the pond shaded at any time?”

That sounds useful, but in practice:

it inflates shade presence
it ignores duration and intensity
it often saturates near high values

So two ponds can both have high SCP but:

one is lightly shaded briefly
one is deeply shaded for hours

👉 Yet SCP treats them similarly

Even though SCP and HSF have similar correlations:

HSF
tied to persistent, high-intensity shade
aligns with thermal stress buffering
ecologically meaningful for drying
SCP
tied to any shade occurrence
doesn’t reflect how effective that shade is

👉 Same correlation strength
👉 very different ecological meaning

Another red flag with SCP

Look at this:

july_scp vs imp_100 = 0.48
july_scp vs veg_mean_cover = 0.43

SCP is:

moderately tied to landscape
moderately tied to vegetation
strongly tied to temperature

👉 It’s drifting toward being a blended, non-specific variable

That weakens PCA interpretation.

So far, HSF is the best option, but still trying others. 

