Answer:

shade
canopy
impervious surroundings
vegetation
pond size and exposure

So in your dataset:

👉 july_water_air is downstream of your other variables

That makes it a derived state variable, even if it has causal meaning in physics.

Why that matters for PCA

If you include it, PCA will do this:

find the strongest variance signal
which is likely temperature
and then align PC1 around it

So instead of discovering:

canopy + shade + vegetation gradients

you’ll get:

“hot ponds vs cool ponds”

Which you already know.

Plus the other water value (av_hrs_water_july_mintomax) can still be perceived as a driver anyway. 


